{"content":[{"c":["MATTANIAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":[" 1. Last king of Judah, whom King Nebuchadnezzar of Babylon enthroned in place of his nephew Jehoiachin; his name subsequently was changed to Zedekiah (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.24.17","r":"2Kgs.24.17","rawR":"2Kgs.24.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.24.17","value":"2Kgs.24.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 24:17"},"), and as such he was known in the other references to him in 2 Kings, 2 Chronicles, and Jeremiah. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Zedekiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Zedekiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Zedekiah_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Zedekiah"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 2. Asaph’s descendant, named among the Levites living in postexilic Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.15","r":"1Chr.9.15","rawR":"1Chr.9.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.15","value":"1Chr.9.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.17,22","r":"Neh.11.17,22","rawR":"Neh.11.17,22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.17,22","value":"Neh.11.17,22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:17, 22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.8,35","r":"Neh.12.8,35","rawR":"Neh.12.8,35","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.8,35","value":"Neh.12.8,35"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:8, 35"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 3. Heman’s son, who helped lead music in the sanctuary during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.25.4,16","r":"1Chr.25.4,16","rawR":"1Chr.25.4,16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.25.4,16","value":"1Chr.25.4,16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 25:4, 16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 4. Levite of the sons of Asaph, who was an ancestor of Jahaziel, a messenger of God in the days of King Jehoshaphat (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.20.14","r":"2Chr.20.14","rawR":"2Chr.20.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.20.14","value":"2Chr.20.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 20:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 5. Another Levite of the sons of Asaph who helped cleanse the temple during King Hezekiah’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.29.13","r":"2Chr.29.13","rawR":"2Chr.29.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.29.13","value":"2Chr.29.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 29:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[" 6–9. Four men of Israel who were exhorted by Ezra to divorce their foreign wives during the postexilic era (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.26-27,30,37","r":"Ezra.10.26-27,30,37","rawR":"Ezra.10.26-27,30,37","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.26-27,30,37","value":"Ezra.10.26-27,30,37"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:26-27, 30, 37"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["10. One of the gatekeepers at the time of the dedication of the reconstructed wall of Jerusalem in Nehemiah’s day (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.25","r":"Neh.12.25","rawR":"Neh.12.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.25","value":"Neh.12.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["11. Grandfather of Hanan, a treasurer of the temple storehouse in Nehemiah’s day (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.13.13","r":"Neh.13.13","rawR":"Neh.13.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.13.13","value":"Neh.13.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 13:13"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Mattaniah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 24:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.24.17","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.24.17","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.24.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.15"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:17, 22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.17,22","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.17,22","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.17,22"},{"anchorText":"12:8, 35","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.8,35","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.8,35","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.8,35"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 25:4, 16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.25.4,16","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.25.4,16","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.25.4,16"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 20:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.20.14","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.20.14","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.20.14"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 29:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.29.13","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.29.13","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.29.13"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:26-27, 30, 37","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.26-27,30,37","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.26-27,30,37","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.26-27,30,37"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.25","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.25","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.25"},{"anchorText":"Neh 13:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.13.13","rawQueryValue":"Neh.13.13","sourceRefExact":"Neh.13.13"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f76373b3886d8a4d09d2ca82871b3498d1367e6cbb1a27a5a181040e1dc0c1bd","sourceItemName":"Mattaniah","sourceItemOrder":173,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Mattaniah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Mattaniah","title":"Mattaniah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}